# Metal hit SFX (MG clank)

When adding **metal** collidable objects (buildings, props, wreckage, railings, etc.), tag the Rapier rigid body so MG hits play the metal clank:

```js
RAPIER.RigidBodyDesc.fixed() // or .dynamic()
  .setTranslation(...)
  .setUserData({ mat: 'metal' })
```

`match.js` `onMgHit` reads `body.userData?.mat === 'metal'` and calls `sfx.ricochet()`. Tanks clank via their own path (damage); do not rely on omitting the tag for tanks.

## Do

- Tag hangars, warehouses, barrels, ships, ironwork — any surface that should clang
- Use the exact string `'metal'` (not `Metal` / `steel`)

## Don't

- Hardcode body handles in a Set for metal SFX
- Assume visual metalness alone triggers the sound — only `userData.mat`
